            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="Legion Primus Medicae Consul" id="hq-consul-medicae" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="hq-consul-medicae-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="35" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legion Primus Medicae Consul" id="hq-consul-medicae-rule" hidden="false">
                  <description>Equipped with a Narthecium; Legion Support Officer and Sacred Trust. Counts as an Apothecary for Armoury restrictions and may purchase a Reductor normally. Sacred Trust: in a mission using Victory Points, whenever a friendly Legiones Astartes Infantry or Jump Infantry unit with a model within 6" is completely destroyed by the enemy, roll a D6. On 5+, the Primus Medicae's player gains 50 Victory Points. A unit for which Victory Points are recovered through the Primus Medicae's Reductor may not also generate Victory Points through Sacred Trust.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <entryLinks>
                <entryLink import="true" name="Narthecium" id="hq-consul-medicae-n" type="selectionEntry" targetId="gear-hq-narthecium" hidden="false" defaultAmount="1">
                  <constraints>
                    <constraint id="hq-consul-medicae-n-min" type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" automatic="true" />
                    <constraint id="hq-consul-medicae-n-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
                  </constraints>
                </entryLink>
                <entryLink import="true" name="Reductor" id="hq-consul-medicae-r" type="selectionEntry" targetId="gear-hq-reductor" hidden="false">
                  <constraints>
                    <constraint id="hq-consul-medicae-r-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
                  </constraints>
                  <costs>
                    <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" />
                  </costs>
                </entryLink>
              </entryLinks>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="Legion Primus Nullificator Consul" id="hq-consul-null" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="hq-consul-null-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="25" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legion Primus Nullificator Consul" id="hq-consul-null-rule" hidden="false">
                  <description>Replace the Chainsword with an Aether-shock Maul. Psyker (Mastery Level 1), Legion Support Officer, Adamantium Will, Hexagrammic Wards and Credo Annihilato. Psychic powers may only be selected from Sanctic Daemonology. Aether-shock Maul: Power Weapon; against Psykers and models with Daemon it always wounds on 2+. Hexagrammic Wards: an enemy Psyker using a power which directly targets the Nullificator or a unit he has joined suffers -1 Leadership for that Psychic test. Credo Annihilato: the Nullificator and any unit he joins have Preferred Enemy (Daemons).</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <entryLinks>
                <entryLink import="true" name="Mandatory Cataphractii Terminator Armour" id="hq-consul-null-cat" type="selectionEntry" targetId="gear-hq-cataphractii" hidden="false" defaultAmount="1">
                  <constraints>
                    <constraint id="hq-consul-null-cat-min" type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" automatic="true" />
                    <constraint id="hq-consul-null-cat-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
                  </constraints>
                  <costs>
                    <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="25" />
                  </costs>
                </entryLink>
              </entryLinks>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="Legion Vigilator Consul" id="hq-consul-vigilator" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="hq-consul-vigilator-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="35" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legion Vigilator Consul" id="hq-consul-vigilator-rule" hidden="false">
                  <description>Equipped with a Bolter and Cameleoline; Scout, Stealth and Sabotage. Special Issue Ammunition: may use the Special Issue Ammunition profiles in this army list with his Bolter, overriding the normal Seeker-only restriction. Sabotage: after both armies deploy but before the first turn, nominate one enemy unit, vehicle or fortification on the battlefield; an Independent Character may only be selected if part of another unit. The target suffers D6 Strength 5 AP6 hits; against vehicles or fortifications use the lowest Armour Value. Casualties do not cause Morale or Pinning tests. Restrictions: no Boarding Shield, Power Fist, Thunder Hammer, Lightning Claws, Bike, Jetbike or Terminator Armour.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <selectionEntries>
                <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="Scout Armour (replaces Power Armour)" id="hq-consul-vigilator-scoutarmour" hidden="false" import="true">
                  <constraints>
                    <constraint id="hq-consul-vigilator-scoutarmour-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
                  </constraints>
                  <costs>
                    <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" />
                  </costs>
                  <rules>
                    <rule name="Scout Armour" id="hq-consul-vigilator-scout-rule" hidden="false">
                      <description>Replacing Power Armour with Scout Armour at no cost additionally grants Infiltrate and Move Through Cover.</description>
                    </rule>
                  </rules>
                </selectionEntry>
              </selectionEntries>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" name="Legion Praevian Consul" id="hq-consul-praevian" hidden="false" import="true">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="hq-consul-praevian-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="35" />
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Legion Praevian Consul" id="hq-consul-praevian-rule" hidden="false">
                  <description>Equipped with Cortex Controller and Cortex Designator; Legion Support Officer, Master of Cybernetica and Legion Inductees. Restrictions: no Jump Pack, Space Marine Bike, Jetbike or any Terminator Armour. Cortex Designator: when the Praevian scores one or more successful To Hit rolls with a shooting weapon against an enemy unit, his attached Battle-Automata Maniple gains Preferred Enemy against that unit until the end of the current player turn; no unsaved Wound is required. Master of Cybernetica: must be accompanied by a Castellax or Vorax Battle-Automata Maniple purchased from the Mechanicum Army List; the Maniple occupies no additional FOC slot and together they count as one HQ selection. The Praevian begins attached and may not voluntarily leave while any Automata remain alive; the Maniple may not take Paragon of Metal. If the Praevian dies, normal Cybernetica Cortex and Programmed Behaviour apply. Legion Inductees: before deployment choose the Praevian's Legiones Astartes rule, Furious Charge, Tank Hunters or Scout for the Maniple for the battle. If Scout is chosen, the Praevian also gains Scout while attached.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Armour Replacement (counts toward 100 pt Armoury limit)" id="hq-centurion-armour" hidden="false">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="hq-centurion-armour-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" />
          </constraints>
          <entryLinks>
            <entryLink import="true" name="Artificer Armour" id="hq-centurion-art" type="selectionEntry" targetId="gear-hq-artificer" hidden="false">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="hq-centurion-art-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="20" />
              </costs>
            </entryLink>
            <entryLink import="true" name="Terminator Armour" id="hq-centurion-term" type="selectionEntry" targetId="gear-hq-terminator" hidden="false">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="hq-centurion-term-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="25" />
              </costs>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
